--TEST--
An anonymous function written in a `Core\Task::afterResponse` call cannot change the response -- a status, a header, a redirect, a cookie, a body method, `slotted` or any session write is a compile error there, in a nested anonymous function too, while an `echo` compiles -- `rule:concurrency/deferred-work-cannot-write-the-response`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// This work runs after the response was sent. Each call below changes the
// response, so each one is a compile error.
Core\Task::afterResponse(fn(): void => {
    Core\Response::setStatus(500);
    Core\Response::setHeader("X-Shop", "1");
    Core\Response::redirect("/shop");
    Core\Response::addCookie("sid", "abc");
    Core\Response::text("body");
    Core\Response::slotted();
    Core\Session::regenerate();
});

// Every session write is a compile error here, for a visitor with a session too.
Core\Task::afterResponse(fn(): void => {
    array<secret bytes> $ring = [Core\Crypto::generateKey()];
    secret string $token = "sk-live-7";
    Core\Session::setShortLived("cart", 3);
    Core\Session::setLongLived("theme", "dark");
    Core\Session::setShortLivedSecret("refresh", $token, $ring);
    Core\Session::setLongLivedSecret("device", $token, $ring);
    Core\Session::remove("cart");
    Core\Session::clearShortLived();
    Core\Session::clearLongLived();
    Core\Session::clearAll();
});

// An anonymous function inside the work runs after the response too.
Core\Task::afterResponse(fn(): void => {
    var $inner = fn(): void => { Core\Response::json(1); };
});

// The work may still write its own output.
Core\Task::afterResponse(fn(): void => {
    echo "receipt sent\n";
});
Core\Response::setHeader("X-Blog", "1");
--EXPECT--

